# LOAD-BEARING SAVE FIXTURES — md5 manifest
#
# ‼‼ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. On 2026-08-11 the SAME hazard cost three separate results in one day:
#   1. the `#24-teachmsgstall` "cheap repro" stopped reproducing — `magma_door.ss1` had been
#      re-captured by a `magmatravel` success hours after the failures were measured on it;
#   2. KI-50 was written up as "the chapter wins 1 in 3" — a RATE — when all three losing runs
#      were byte-identical and the single win had been on different bytes of the same filename;
#   3. the KI-52 live A/B was VOIDED — the fixture was pinned *after* a still-in-flight background
#      job had overwritten it, and only the copy was md5'd, never compared to the failing run's.
# Every one of them is "same name, different bytes". Resolving to be careful did not work; this
# file plus `verify_fixtures.py` makes the check mechanical.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   PYTHONUTF8=1 py -3.12 verify_fixtures.py            # before trusting any fixture-based result
#   PYTHONUTF8=1 py -3.12 verify_fixtures.py --update    # ONLY when you intend a fixture to change
#
# ‼ A save that any DRIVER re-captures is a CACHE, not a fixture. `magma_door.ss1` is rewritten by
# `--driver magmatravel` on every success and `magma_1f_fail.ss1` by `--driver magmahideout` on
# every failure — they are listed as VOLATILE and are expected to drift. Anything you need to hold
# still must be copied to a name nothing writes to.
#
# format:  <md5>  <filename>  <VOLATILE|PINNED>  <what it is / what it is for>

69ac95c6e05a25a5206e8cac6ce0a964  post_grind_L60.ss1  PINNED  ⛔⛔ **A DEAD BRANCH — DO NOT GRIND FROM IT AND DO NOT REPAIR IT (ruled 2026-09-17, `06-DECISIONS-LOG.md`).** It BRANCHED STRAIGHT OFF `post_training.ss1` and skipped the entire §Ch24 prep chain, so its 13 extra levels cost a ~700,000-frame Abandoned Ship trip plus four teaches to make usable — while `post_ch24ready.ss1` is ALREADY prepped and reaches L75 in ~3.7 h. ✅ KEEP IT: it is the ancestor of `grind_stall_ppzero.ss1`, the `#24-grindppstall` failing arm. —— *the original entry:* PINNED  ⛔⛔ **NO ICE BEAM AND NO FLY — THIS IS A DIFFERENT LINEAGE FROM THE §Ch24 FIXTURES (measured 2026-09-16).** Its Wailord carries **Water Spout** where `post_ch24_atdoor.ss1`'s carries **ICE BEAM**, and its Swellow has **Peck/Wing Attack** where the other has **FLY**. Sceptile has Slam where the other has Aerial Ace, and Mightyena has Tackle where the other has Strength. ⛔⛔ **MECHANISM CORRECTED 2026-09-17 — THE GRIND OVERWROTE NOTHING; THE LINEAGES DIVERGED EARLIER.** *(This said “the grind learned level-up moves OVER the curated set”.)* **MEASURED:** the ancestor `post_training.ss1` (L47-51, the save `post_grind_L60.ss1` was produced FROM) already carries the identical move NAMES — Wailord `Dive, Surf, Water Spout, Waterfall`, Swellow `Peck, Wing Attack, Aerial Ace, Quick Attack`, Sceptile `Rock Smash, Strength, Leaf Blade, Slam`, Mightyena `Tackle, Crunch, Take Down, Bite`. ⇒ **this lineage NEVER HAD Ice Beam or Fly to lose**; it diverged from the Ice-Beam lineage BEFORE that ancestor, and `Water Spout` is simply Wailord's natural **L44** level-up move. ⛔⛔ **RETRACTED 2026-09-17 — REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT ON THE §Ch24 LINEAGE.** *(This said the bot “DECLINES level-up moves” and that “a taught move will NOT be undone by grinding”.)* **IT IS NOT A RULE, AND THE OBJECTION I USED IT TO DISMISS WAS CORRECT.** Wailord **LOST ICE BEAM TO HYDRO PUMP AT EXACTLY L59** — the very level I cited as proof it would not:  post_e4grind_L57.ss1 / L57 / Dive, / Surf, / Ice / Beam, / Waterfall  post_e4grind_L59.ss1 / L59 / Dive, / Surf, / Hydro / Pump, / Waterfall / <<< / -Ice / Beam / +Hydro / Pump
  ⭐ **THE REAL MECHANISM** (`#24-learnhmcoverage`, now fixed): `which_move_should_be_replaced` decides per case, and its type-coverage census was built from the **replaceable** slots, which **EXCLUDE HMs**. Wailord's three Water moves are all HMs (Dive/Surf/Waterfall), so the census read `[Ice]`, Hydro Pump looked like **a type we LACK**, and the policy “freed the weakest slot to gain coverage” — spending the team's only Ice move on a FOURTH Water move. ‼ **THE SAME CODE EXPLAINS THE OBSERVATION THAT MISLED ME:** on the `post_grind_L60` lineage that slot held **Water Spout** — a TM, so non-HM — the census read `[Water]`, Hydro Pump was REDUNDANT and weaker (150 vs 120), and it correctly DECLINED. Same code, same level, opposite outcome, decided purely by which slot happened to be replaceable. ⇒ I watched the policy work correctly on one party and wrote down a universal law. —— *the retracted text:* ⭐⭐ **AND THE OPPOSITE OF MY CLAIM IS TRUE, WHICH IS THE USEFUL PART: THE BOT DECLINES LEVEL-UP MOVES.** Wailord crossed **L52 (Amnesia)** and **L59 (Hydro Pump)** during that L47→L60 grind and kept all four of its moves. ⇒ **a taught move will NOT be undone by grinding** — which is the strongest objection to the repair plan, refuted by measurement rather than argument. ‼ Corroborated from the learnsets: **no battler learns ANYTHING between L61 and L75** (last level-up moves: Wailord/Sceptile L59, Mightyena L52, Swellow L49, Zigzagoon L41, Castform L30 — read from `modules/data/species.json`, with a control that printed Wailord's full learnset and found `Water Spout` at L44 as expected). ⛔ **DO NOT “FIX” THE GRIND TO STOP OVERWRITING MOVES — there is no such defect.**  **Ice Beam is the designated DRAKE counter** (Flygon has LEVITATE, so Ice is the only super-effective type reachable on it) and cost two work items to teach (`#24-icebeamtrip`, `#24-icebeamteach`); **Fly is how §Ch24 reaches the League at all.** ‼ **AND THE ORIGINAL VERIFICATION COULD NOT HAVE SEEN THIS:** this row says “Verified by RELOADING the file (`probe_anchor_inventory.py`)” — and that probe **does not print movesets**, a caveat the docs already record for the OTHER fixture. ⇒ do NOT use this save as a §Ch24 start state, and do not assume grinding it produces a gauntlet-ready party. See `#24-fixturelineage`. —— ⭐ THE L60 PARTY. All four battlers at **L60** (Wailord/Mightyena/Sceptile/Swellow) + the mules Zigzagoon L19 / Castform L36, standing on VICTORY_ROAD_1F (15,39) — the training tile — with all 8 badges and HP 984/992 (99%). Verified by RELOADING the file (`probe_anchor_inventory.py --filter post_grind_L60`), not by a driver's log. Produced 2026-09-07 by `--driver ch24grind` from `post_training.ss1`: **623 battles, 0 whiteouts, 1782 s** (~30 min at the measured 1032 f/s). ‼ Its purpose is to test §Ch24 at the level the SIMULATION says clears Glacia — turning that estimate into a drive. ⛔ It is PINNED, not VOLATILE, because `ch24grind`'s capture REFUSES to overwrite an existing file; nothing rewrites this name. ⭐ A CHECKPOINT LADDER exists beside it — `post_grind_L49/51/53/55/57/59.ss1` (ODD levels only; the grind steps 2 levels at a time) — so a future session can resume at any level instead of re-grinding 30 minutes. ‼ `post_grind_FINAL.ss1` was byte-identical to this file and was DELETED rather than committed twice; an earlier version of this row claimed it exists, and a Tier 2 cold-start audit caught it.
