2f517f1f790b0151af9a7837ac493e4e  post_training.ss1  PINNED  **THE §Ch23 TRAINING OUTPUT FIXTURE — THE FIRST STATE THIS PROJECT HAS EVER HAD THAT IS *READY FOR WALLY*.** ⛔⛔ **IT IS *NOT* READY FOR THE ELITE FOUR, AND THIS ROW SAID SO FOR ONE COMMIT — CORRECTED 2026-09-04 AFTER THE EVIDENCE CONTRADICTED IT.** This party beat Wally (ace **L45**) at the cost of **two faints and 67% HP**; the Elite Four run **L46-58** and Wallace's team is **L55-58** with four Full Restores and a Recover/Sitrus Milotic. L47 was chosen because it is the highest target AFFORDABLE on 1F and Mightyena's Crunch level — never because it clears the League. ⇒ the remaining gap is meant to be closed on **B1F after Wally**. ‼ *An overclaim in a fixture row is the most expensive kind: it is what a future session reads to decide the party is ready.* Captured 2026-09-04 by `--driver ch23train` with `CH23_CAPTURE` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (`ACCEPTANCE: PASS`, **battles=132, whiteouts=0**), so the file's EXISTENCE is the acceptance record. Probe-verified (`probe_anchor_inventory --filter post_training`): OVERWORLD **VICTORY_ROAD_1F (15,39)**, badges=12345678, party 6 — **Sceptile L51, Zigzagoon L19, Swellow L47, Wailord L47, Mightyena L47, Castform L36**, HP 754/796 (95%). ⭐⭐ **MIGHTYENA KNOWS CRUNCH** — the run log carries the literal `MIGHTYENA learned CRUNCH!`, and that is the binding constraint of the whole arc: Emerald has NO Dark TM, so a Mightyena that reached 47 without the level-up learn could never answer Phoebe's Ghosts. ⭐ **Wailmer EVOLVED INTO WAILORD at L41** en route, and the identity tracking survived it (PID `FA51ECF3` unchanged) — which is exactly why this leg asserts on PID and never on species or slot. ⛔ **THIS FIXTURE ONLY EXISTS BECAUSE OF KI-84.** The first attempt at the same grind, from the same start, produced **8 battles** and stalled at Wailmer L41 / Swellow L42, because `train_team(slots={i})` with `i != 0` runs ONE spin-batch and returns as if finished (it re-reads `party[i]` by index after SWAPPING that mon to slot 0). The leg now rotates to slot 0 first and calls `train_team(slots={0})`. ⚠ **(15,39) IS AN ENCOUNTER TILE** — `'Cave'`, one step from the 1F entrance warp — so a run resuming here can meet a wild Pokémon on its first step; that is intended (it is the training spot), not a defect. ⚠ Zigzagoon L19 and Castform L36 are DELIBERATELY untrained bench (typing, not levels, is their problem) — they are still in the party and a faint cascade can send them in. ⚠ HP is 95%, not 100%: heal before Wally.
